{"The new useIsGrafanaPromRuleEditable hook references ctx.hasPermissionInMetadata(...), but ctx is not shown as being defined within the hook scope. This will throw at runtime if ctx is not available from a hook/context in this module, and if it is available, it should be included in memo dependencies.": 0.46636301279067993, "useAllRulerRuleAbilities now accepts rule as optional, but still calls helpers like rulerRuleType.grafana.rule(rule) and isPluginProvidedRule(rule). These helpers may not safely handle undefined, which could cause runtime errors and accidental permission escalation/denial when rule data is missing.": 0.7923964858055115, "The loader no longer renders 'creating/deleting' transitional list items (it now renders only Prometheus-provided rules). If Prometheus data lags behind rule CRUD operations, users may lose feedback about in-progress state or recently deleted rules.": 0.849640965461731}